`,p.jsxs(l.p,{children:[p.jsx(l.strong,{children:"How does an abstraction influence a person's ability to decompose programming problems?"})," A central task in programming is to take a problem (",p.jsxs("q",{children:["build a website to do ",p.jsx("i",{children:"X"})]}),", ",p.jsxs("q",{children:["analyze ",p.jsx("i",{children:"Y"})," feature of a dataset"]}),") and break it down into pieces that correspond to features of the language or library at hand (e.g., for loops or ",p.jsx("code",{children:"List.map"}),"). A key challenge is to understand what it means to ",p.jsx("q",{children:"think with"})," an abstraction, so one could argue why an abstraction would be better or worse for decomposition."]}),`
