`,p.jsxs(l.p,{children:[p.jsx(l.strong,{children:"How can we reliably create assessments that are valid measures of skill?"})," Performance on a test should ideally correlate to performance on a real-world skill that we care about, but such ",p.jsx("q",{children:"validated instruments"})," are difficult and time-consuming to create. I am interested in methods for computationally generating assessments grounded in data that improves the validity of the questions. See: ",p.jsx(l.a,{href:"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1145/3287324.3287504",children:"Quizius"})," (2019)."]}),`
